IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `colc-common`
IMPORT `colc-levy`

-- UNOFFICIAL. Based on content from the South Australian Legislation website (State of South Australia, CC BY 4.0), taken
-- from the Open Australian Legal Corpus (CC BY 4.0); each text may be out of date.
--
-- Cases for colc-levy.l4: the Emergency Services Funding Act 1998 and the Remissions--Land Regulations 2014. Every
-- expected value is worked by hand from the deposited text, with the arithmetic in the comment above the assertion.
-- The levy and the reg 7(1a) and 7(2) amounts are ILLUSTRATIVE: the deposit holds neither the declared levy nor the
-- two formulas. Clock for the regulative rule: days from service of the notice.

§ `Cases -- the emergency services levy on the home`

§§ `Builders`

GIVEN `the year` IS A NUMBER, `residential` IS A BOOLEAN, `levy` IS A NUMBER, `concession amount` IS A NUMBER, `general amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Land under the notice of levy`
`land for` `the year` `residential` `levy` `concession amount` `general amount` MEANS
    `Land under the notice of levy` WITH
        `the levy's financial year begins in` IS `the year`
        `the land is residential land` IS `residential`
        `the amount of the levy` IS `levy`
        `the regulation 7(2) remission for the land` IS `concession amount`
        `the regulation 7(1a) remission for the land` IS `general amount`

GIVEN `interest` IS AN `Interest in land`, `share` IS A NUMBER, `card` IS A `Commonwealth card or payment`, `in the window` IS A BOOLEAN, `principal place of residence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Owner of the home`
`an owner with` `interest` `share` `card` `in the window` `principal place of residence` MEANS
    `Owner of the home` WITH
        `interest at 12.01 a.m. on 1 July` IS `interest`
        `share of the land` IS `share`
        `card or payment` IS `card`
        `falls within a class on the date of issue, on the payment date or at any time between` IS `in the window`
        `the Minister is satisfied the land was the principal place of residence on 1 July` IS `principal place of residence`

GIVEN `asker` IS AN `Owner of the home`, `spouse co-owns` IS A BOOLEAN, `spouse` IS AN `Owner of the home`
GIVETH AN `Owners of the home`
`owners` `asker` `spouse co-owns` `spouse` MEANS
    `Owners of the home` WITH
        `the owner asking` IS `asker`
        `a spouse or domestic partner co-owns the land` IS `spouse co-owns`
        `the spouse or domestic partner` IS `spouse`

`freehold` MEANS `the holder of the estate in fee simple, the land not being subject to a life estate`

-- 2024/25, residential, levy $300, reg 7(2) amount $200, reg 7(1a) amount $50 (all illustrative).
`the 2024/25 notice` MEANS `land for` 2024 TRUE 300 200 50

-- Nobody: used where there is no co-owning spouse.
`nobody` MEANS `an owner with` `a tenant or other occupier holding none of these interests` 0 `none of these` FALSE FALSE

-- Margaret: sole freehold owner, Pensioner Concession Card throughout, her home on 1 July.
`Margaret` MEANS `an owner with` `freehold` 1 `a Pensioner Concession Card` TRUE TRUE
`Margaret alone` MEANS `owners` `Margaret` FALSE `nobody`

§§ `s 3(1), s 15 -- owner and liability`

#ASSERT `the holder of that interest is the owner of the land` `freehold`
-- s 3(1)(a)(i): the life tenant is the owner, not the holder of the fee simple subject to it.
#ASSERT `the holder of that interest is the owner of the land` `the holder of a life estate in land granted in fee simple`
#ASSERT NOT (`the holder of that interest is the owner of the land` `the holder of the estate in fee simple in land subject to another person's life estate`)
-- s 3(1)(e)(i), (f).
#ASSERT `the holder of that interest is the owner of the land` `the person entitled to occupy land held from the Crown under a lease, licence or agreement to purchase`
#ASSERT `the holder of that interest is the owner of the land` `the person entitled to occupy land held under a shack lease`
-- A tenant is not the owner, so not liable (s 15(1)).
#ASSERT NOT (`the owner is liable for the levy` `nobody`)
-- s 15(2): jointly and severally liable: the Commissioner can look to a half owner for the whole $300.
#ASSERT `the most the Commissioner can recover from one owner` 300 (`an owner with` `freehold` 0.5 `none of these` FALSE TRUE) EQUALS 300
#ASSERT `the most the Commissioner can recover from one owner` 300 `nobody` EQUALS 0

§§ `s 16(2)(d) -- the payment date`

-- Served 1 August 2024; payment date 29 August 2024: 28 days.
#ASSERT `the payment date is at least 28 days after the notice was served` (YearMonthDay 2024 8 1) (YearMonthDay 2024 8 29)
-- 28 August 2024: 27 days, too early.
#ASSERT NOT (`the payment date is at least 28 days after the notice was served` (YearMonthDay 2024 8 1) (YearMonthDay 2024 8 28))

§§ `reg 3, reg 6 -- who gets the concession holders' remission`

#ASSERT `is the relevant financial year` 2024
#ASSERT NOT (`is the relevant financial year` 2025)
-- reg 6(5)(f): the Commonwealth Seniors Health Card counts here (unlike the water rates remission).
#ASSERT `is a class set out in regulation 6(5)` `a Commonwealth Seniors Health Card`
-- reg 6(5)(j) names the Community Development Program; the Community Development Employment Project or Remote Jobs
-- and Economic Development Program payments (named in the cost of living regulations) are not in the list (finding 10).
#ASSERT `is a class set out in regulation 6(5)` `payments under the Community Development Program`
#ASSERT NOT (`is a class set out in regulation 6(5)` `payments under the Community Development Employment Project or the Remote Jobs and Economic Development Program`)
#ASSERT NOT (`is a class set out in regulation 6(5)` `none of these`)

-- reg 6(1): Margaret holds residential land, her principal place of residence, a reg 6(5)(a) card in the window.
#ASSERT `the owner is entitled to the regulation 6 remission in their own right` `the 2024/25 notice` `Margaret`
-- reg 6(1)(c): a card held only outside the window between issue and payment dates does not count.
#ASSERT NOT (`the owner is entitled to the regulation 6 remission in their own right` `the 2024/25 notice` (`an owner with` `freehold` 1 `a Pensioner Concession Card` FALSE TRUE))
-- reg 6(1)(b), (6): the Minister not satisfied it was her principal place of residence on 1 July.
#ASSERT NOT (`the owner is entitled to the regulation 6 remission in their own right` `the 2024/25 notice` (`an owner with` `freehold` 1 `a Pensioner Concession Card` TRUE FALSE))
-- reg 3: other financial years are outside the deposited remissions.
#ASSERT NOT (`the owner is entitled to the regulation 6 remission in their own right` (`land for` 2025 TRUE 300 200 50) `Margaret`)

-- reg 6(4): Ken and Lee, a married couple owning half each, both living there; only Lee has a card. Both are
-- entitled.
`Ken` MEANS `an owner with` `freehold` 0.5 `none of these` FALSE TRUE
`Lee` MEANS `an owner with` `freehold` 0.5 `a Pensioner Concession Card` TRUE TRUE
`Ken and Lee` MEANS `owners` `Ken` TRUE `Lee`

#ASSERT NOT (`the owner is entitled to the regulation 6 remission in their own right` `the 2024/25 notice` `Ken`)
#ASSERT `regulation 6(4) applies to the couple` `the 2024/25 notice` `Ken and Lee`
#ASSERT `the owner asking is entitled to the regulation 6 remission` `the 2024/25 notice` `Ken and Lee`
#ASSERT `the spouse or domestic partner is entitled to the regulation 6 remission` `the 2024/25 notice` `Ken and Lee`

-- reg 6(4)(a): Lee's card, but the land is not Lee's principal place of residence: no couple rule; Lee is not entitled
-- in her own right either, so neither is.
`Lee living elsewhere` MEANS `an owner with` `freehold` 0.5 `a Pensioner Concession Card` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 6(4) applies to the couple` `the 2024/25 notice` (`owners` `Ken` TRUE `Lee living elsewhere`))
#ASSERT NOT (`the owner asking is entitled to the regulation 6 remission` `the 2024/25 notice` (`owners` `Ken` TRUE `Lee living elsewhere`))

§§ `reg 7, reg 8 -- the amounts`

-- reg 7(2) $200, then reg 7(3) $46 from the $100 left (reg 8): $246 for the whole land.
#ASSERT `the concession holders' remission for the whole land` `the 2024/25 notice` EQUALS 246
-- A smaller levy of $220: $200, then only the $20 left of the further $46 (finding 12): $220.
#ASSERT `the concession holders' remission for the whole land` (`land for` 2024 TRUE 220 200 50) EQUALS 220
-- A reg 7(2) amount above the levy is held to the levy: $300, and nothing further.
#ASSERT `the concession holders' remission for the whole land` (`land for` 2024 TRUE 300 400 50) EQUALS 300

-- Margaret alone: 1 x 246 under reg 6; nothing under reg 5A (reg 5A(2)).
#ASSERT `the levy remitted for the owner asking and a co-owning spouse or partner` `the 2024/25 notice` `Margaret alone` EQUALS `the levy remitted for us` 246 0
#ASSERT `our share of the levy after the remissions` `the 2024/25 notice` `Margaret alone` EQUALS 54
-- A sole owner with no card: the general remission, 1 x 50; she bears 300 - 50 = 250.
`Nora alone` MEANS `owners` (`an owner with` `freehold` 1 `none of these` FALSE TRUE) FALSE `nobody`
#ASSERT `the levy remitted for the owner asking and a co-owning spouse or partner` `the 2024/25 notice` `Nora alone` EQUALS `the levy remitted for us` 0 50
#ASSERT `our share of the levy after the remissions` `the 2024/25 notice` `Nora alone` EQUALS 250
-- Ken and Lee: both halves carry the reg 6 remission: (0.5 + 0.5) x 246 = 246; they bear 300 - 246 = 54.
#ASSERT `the levy remitted for the owner asking and a co-owning spouse or partner` `the 2024/25 notice` `Ken and Lee` EQUALS `the levy remitted for us` 246 0
#ASSERT `our share of the levy after the remissions` `the 2024/25 notice` `Ken and Lee` EQUALS 54
-- Ken has the card himself, Lee lives elsewhere: Ken's half carries reg 6 (0.5 x 246 = 123); Lee's half, not entitled,
-- carries reg 5A(3) (0.5 x 50 = 25): 148 in all; they bear 300 - 148 = 152.
`Ken with a card` MEANS `an owner with` `freehold` 0.5 `a Pensioner Concession Card` TRUE TRUE
`Lee living elsewhere, no card` MEANS `an owner with` `freehold` 0.5 `none of these` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `the levy remitted for the owner asking and a co-owning spouse or partner` `the 2024/25 notice` (`owners` `Ken with a card` TRUE `Lee living elsewhere, no card`) EQUALS `the levy remitted for us` 123 25
#ASSERT `our share of the levy after the remissions` `the 2024/25 notice` (`owners` `Ken with a card` TRUE `Lee living elsewhere, no card`) EQUALS 152
-- Omar owns half with his brother, who has a card (reg 6); Omar has none: reg 5A(3), 0.5 x 50 = 25; Omar's half of the
-- levy, 150, less 25 = 125. The brother's entitlement is not asked: had he no card, reg 5A(1) with s 15(2) would give
-- Omar the same 0.5 x 50 (finding 14), so the answer is the same either way.
`Omar with his brother` MEANS `owners` (`an owner with` `freehold` 0.5 `none of these` FALSE TRUE) FALSE `nobody`
#ASSERT `the levy remitted for the owner asking and a co-owning spouse or partner` `the 2024/25 notice` `Omar with his brother` EQUALS `the levy remitted for us` 0 25
#ASSERT `our share of the levy after the remissions` `the 2024/25 notice` `Omar with his brother` EQUALS 125
-- A Seniors Health Card holder gets the reg 6 remission: 246.
#ASSERT `the levy remitted for the owner asking and a co-owning spouse or partner` `the 2024/25 notice` (`owners` (`an owner with` `freehold` 1 `a Commonwealth Seniors Health Card` TRUE TRUE) FALSE `nobody`) EQUALS `the levy remitted for us` 246 0
-- A life tenant is the owner and gets it too.
#ASSERT `the levy remitted for the owner asking and a co-owning spouse or partner` `the 2024/25 notice` (`owners` (`an owner with` `the holder of a life estate in land granted in fee simple` 1 `a Pensioner Concession Card` TRUE TRUE) FALSE `nobody`) EQUALS `the levy remitted for us` 246 0

-- Outside the encoding.
#ASSERT `the levy remitted for the owner asking and a co-owning spouse or partner` (`land for` 2025 TRUE 300 200 50) `Margaret alone` EQUALS `not covered` `the deposited regulations remit the levy for the 2024/2025 financial year only`
#ASSERT `the levy remitted for the owner asking and a co-owning spouse or partner` (`land for` 2024 FALSE 300 200 50) `Margaret alone` EQUALS `not covered` `the land is not residential land, and the remissions for other land are not encoded`
#ASSERT `the levy remitted for the owner asking and a co-owning spouse or partner` `the 2024/25 notice` (`owners` (`an owner with` `the person entitled to occupy land held from the Crown under a lease, licence or agreement to purchase` 1 `a Pensioner Concession Card` TRUE TRUE) FALSE `nobody`) EQUALS `not covered` `the land is held from the Crown, and regulation 5 is not encoded`
-- A tenant is not liable, so nothing is remitted for them.
#ASSERT `the levy remitted for the owner asking and a co-owning spouse or partner` `the 2024/25 notice` (`owners` `nobody` FALSE `nobody`) EQUALS `no remission: not the owner at 12.01 a.m. on 1 July, so not liable for the levy`
#ASSERT `the total remitted` (`the levy remitted for the owner asking and a co-owning spouse or partner` `the 2024/25 notice` `Ken and Lee`) EQUALS 246

§§ `Regulative rule`

-- Margaret pays her $54 on day 20 of the 28 days.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 15(1), s 16(2)(d) -- the owner must pay the levy by the date in the notice` 54 28) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the owner of the land` (`pay the levy to the Commissioner` 54) 20)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- Paying on the payment date itself (day 28) is in time.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 15(1), s 16(2)(d) -- the owner must pay the levy by the date in the notice` 54 28) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the owner of the land` (`pay the levy to the Commissioner` 54) 28)) EQUALS FULFILLED

#TRACE `s 15(1), s 16(2)(d) -- the owner must pay the levy by the date in the notice` 54 28 AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 29)
-- expect: BREACH by `the owner of the land`: s 15(1), s 16(2)(d)

#TRACE `s 15(1), s 16(2)(d) -- the owner must pay the levy by the date in the notice` 54 28 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the owner of the land` DOES `pay the levy to the Commissioner` 30 AT 10
-- expect: still pending: $30 is not the $54 payable
